assistant: Subject: Accept epoch-millisecond created_at in get_order

The vendor's API version 2026-10-01 sends `created_at` as a number of milliseconds since 1970 (e.g. `1792142857943`), not the ISO-8601 string the spec describes. `get_order` ran every value through `Date.parse(String(...))`, which can't read a number string. It returned `NaN`, and the `|| 0` fallback quietly turned that into 1970-01-01. The handler now passes a numeric `created_at` straight to `new Date`, so o-5001 gives `2026-10-16T09:27:37.943Z`. String values go through the same code as before, so the v1 output is unchanged. Typecheck, lint and tests all pass. The `|| 0` fallback is still there, so any other date the code can't read will still show up as 1970 without warning. I didn't change that because it would change v1 behaviour.

